 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? It depends on how thick you painted with oils. A thin layer of oil paint dries pretty fast, but thick build up can take months. Then I' varnish it right after it's dry to the touch, which should be within few weeks. Then varnish every few months until you reach six months. If you' really in a hurry, a quick coat of a thin acrylic gel hood can beat waiting, but it's not permanent. It feel smooth the touch, like freshly varnished floor. Pick up a piece of tape and pull it slowly, if the paint doesn't peel off with it, it's dry.",
